# Example fixture: bulk Si (diamond cubic, conventional 8-atom cell,
# a=5.463 Ang, the correct/expected lattice constant -- unlike
# 15-mlrelax's si_wrong_a.fdf, no deliberate error here). Used to exercise
# stb-amorphize's melt-quench protocol.
#
# Deliberately tiny (8 atoms) with correspondingly tiny --melt-steps/
# --quench-steps in test.sh, purely so the automated smoke test finishes
# quickly -- this is NOT representative of real amorphization quality
# (too few atoms and MD steps for meaningful statistics). The actual
# physics (bond-angle std going from 0 to a large value while the mean
# stays near the tetrahedral angle, matching real amorphous-Si behavior)
# was validated live during planning with a proper 64-atom cell and
# realistic step counts -- see CLAUDE.md's stb-amorphize entry.


NumberOfSpecies    1
NumberofAtoms      8

%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1   14   Si
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

LatticeConstant 1.0 Ang

AtomicCoordinatesFormat  Fractional

%block LatticeVectors
 5.46300000   0.00000000   0.00000000
 0.00000000   5.46300000   0.00000000
 0.00000000   0.00000000   5.46300000
%endblock LatticeVectors

%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
  0.50000000   0.00000000   0.50000000   1
  0.25000000   0.25000000   0.25000000   1
  0.00000000   0.00000000   0.00000000   1
  0.25000000   0.75000000   0.75000000   1
  0.75000000   0.25000000   0.75000000   1
  0.00000000   0.50000000   0.50000000   1
  0.50000000   0.50000000   0.00000000   1
  0.75000000   0.75000000   0.25000000   1
%endblock AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
